<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Comecon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1949">1949</a>–<a href="/years/1991">1991</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Council for Mutual Economic Assistance</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Comecon, the Council for Mutual Economic Assistance, was the economic organisation of the Soviet bloc, founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> in January 1949. It coordinated trade and planning among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, the East European communist states and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, largely on Soviet terms. It was dissolved in June 1991 after the fall of communism in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-europe">Eastern Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/comecon.jpg" alt="Comecon" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Froztbyte · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Comecon.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
